  "id": "COMPOUND:43026 - PROTEIN:5788",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential pathway by which isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside may interact with SNB-78 through a series of target relationships. This compound appears to act as a target for Raji, which in turn is targeted by multiple drugs, including Maplexin A and terbutaline. These drugs are themselves targets of SNB-78, indicating a possible cascade of interactions where isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside influences the activity of intermediate molecules that ultimately engage SNB-78. The shared targeting of Raji by different compounds suggests a possible functional overlap or regulatory mechanism, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the precise role of isocytisoside-7-O-glucoside in this pathway requires further investigation.",
